# Adaptive experience - planner configuration.
#
# By default the AI planner is a deterministic mock (no setup needed). To test
# with a local model instead:
#
#   1. Install Ollama (https://ollama.com) and pull a small model:
#        ollama pull qwen2.5:3b
#   2. Copy this file to `.env`, uncomment the lines below, and restart the dev
#      server.
#   3. Open /adaptive?search=chair, stage products or sort by price, and watch
#      the "AI planner - shadow proposals" panel. Shadow mode (the default, in
#      app/app.config.ts) records what the model *would* do without applying it.
#      Flip aiShadowMode to false there to let the model actually move the UI.
#
# Whatever the model returns is untrusted: the endpoint re-validates it against
# the patch schema and the merger enforces the capability flags, so a bad model
# only ever produces a rejected proposal.
#
# Model note: the provider asks the model for a flat *decision* (one action plus
# a sentence of copy) and expands it into a patch in code. A small local model
# classifies a few signals well but cannot reliably synthesise the nested patch
# itself. qwen2.5:3b follows the decision format; llama3.2:3b tends to return no
# action at all. See FINDINGS.md ("Testing with a local model").

# EXPERIENCE_PLANNER=ollama
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:3b

# A local model on CPU is slower than a hosted one. These raise the server-side
# generation timeout and the client's wait so slow replies still get recorded.
# OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_MS=12000
# EXPERIENCE_PLANNER_TIMEOUT_MS=12000
